invariant: INV-41
file: rsa_ifma_product.h
catches: rsa_ifma_model_test
reason: normalize_digits adds the carry out of the top lane of the top
  register to lane 0 rather than dropping it, so the lanes no longer hold
  their number modulo 2^(52 * lanes). A product's sum is below 2^(52n),
  so its top lane carries nothing and no product shows the change.
  bin/rsa_ifma_model_test's run of normalize_digits on lanes at and
  above 2^52, the top lane among them, sees the number change.

--- old
    rsa_ifma_lanes below = lanes_zero(); // the carries of the register below
--- new
    rsa_ifma_lanes below = lanes_shift_right_52(sum[registers - 1]);
